    "Add at least 3 to 4 dedicated leg sets next week — compound movements like squats or Romanian deadlifts are ideal for muscle building and will help correct the severe volume imbalance quickly.",
    "Maintain your current chest and back progression since both indices rose 3 to 4 points this week; keep the same loading approach and aim for another quality session on each.",
    "Check your biceps loading relative to triceps — if you are using similar rep ranges, consider slightly increasing the weight or adding a set to bring biceps tonnage closer in line with triceps over the coming weeks.",
    "Keep total weekly sets at or above 23 and aim to distribute them more evenly across all muscle groups, with legs taking a proportionally larger share until the imbalance is corrected."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strong upper-body progress this week with chest and back indices both up 3 to 4 points, but legs were severely undertrained at just 1 set — the top priority for next period is substantially increasing leg volume while maintaining current upper-body momentum."
}
